DGX third-party software and corresponding source

This distribution uses third-party libraries under their respective licenses;
the application's Apache-2.0 license does not replace those licenses.
DEPENDENCIES.json lists the resolved packages, versions, declared licenses and
copied notice files. Original notices embedded in source files are retained in
the accompanying corresponding-source.tar.gz archive.
The exact pinned Portfu packages have an owner-confirmed Apache-2.0 grant
recorded in NOTICE-PORTFU; the inventory distinguishes that grant from the
upstream manifests' omitted license declarations.

The DGX full-node and timelord use Rug and gmp-mpfr-sys under LGPL-3.0-or-later,
including the bundled GMP library under its upstream terms. Their use is
covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License. Copies of the GNU LGPL and
GNU GPL are included under dependencies/rug-*/ and dependencies/gmp-mpfr-sys-*/.

The archive at /usr/local/share/dgx/corresponding-source.tar.gz contains the
application source, exact Cargo-vendored dependency source, build scripts,
Cargo.lock and offline Cargo source configuration. It accompanies the binaries
to support the corresponding-source and relinking option in LGPLv3 section
4(d)(0). It also includes sources for MPL and CDDL dependencies if resolved.
The optional CUDA executable has an additional source archive and notices
under /usr/local/share/dgx/cuda and /usr/local/share/licenses/dgx/cuda.

Extract the archive, inspect BUILD-TOOLCHAIN.json, and use the commands and
system build prerequisites in Dockerfile (or docker/Dockerfile.cuda for CUDA).
Cargo accepts --offline with the supplied vendor directory. For example:

  cargo build --offline --locked --release -p dg_xch_cli --bin dgx \
    --no-default-features --features hint,timelord

Use the features and binaries from the Docker stage being rebuilt. Modify the
vendored library sources to rebuild with your own library changes. When doing
so, update the modified file entries in that crate's .cargo-checksum.json to
the new SHA-256 values; the package checksum should remain unchanged. Run Cargo
again to rebuild and relink the application. Rebuilt executables can replace
the originals in a derived image; no DGX signing key or approval is required.
Modification and reverse engineering to debug library modifications are not
restricted by DGX. Redistribution must preserve the applicable third-party
licenses and this corresponding-source access.

Container base-system packages retain their distribution-provided notices in
/usr/share/doc. CUDA toolkit components are subject to NVIDIA's own terms;
the optional CUDA build does not relicense those components as Apache-2.0.
